 "notes": "The header comment still says 'for the farm animals' but the file now covers villager, iron golem and hostile tasks (the AIC_* list includes VILLAGER_MATE, MOVE_THROUGH_VILLAGE, DEFEND_VILLAGE, CREEPER_SWELL, ARROW_ATTACK, BREAK_DOOR, FLEE_SUN and more). Not ported: tame-animal tasks (EntityAIBeg, Sit, FollowOwner, OwnerHurtByTarget, OwnerHurtTarget, TargetNonTamed, OcelotSit, OcelotAttack, LeapAtTarget, RunAroundLikeCrazy); their mobs (wolf, ocelot, horse) are switched off in world.conf. The per-task Java member lists are the standard EntityAIBase overrides each class has, inferred from the task switch structure (ai_should_execute, ai_continue_executing, ai_start, ai_reset, ai_update), not verified method by method. test_paths.c and test_villagers.c were not opened to confirm which ai.c functions they reach. Task lists hold AI_MAX_ENTRIES 16 (the villager's 15 plus the leash's move-towards-restriction; task_slot stops the program past it); EntityAIMoveThroughVillage's door list lives once per living (mtv_visited_doors), not in every task entry (lane worldmem). lane/idxentity: the iron golem's navigator never swims; EntityAIBreakDoor breaks the door on HARD at 240."
}
